{
  "_id": {
    "$oid": "68f5d3f495fc82365e4cd5af"
  },
  "title": "Let’s Practice English Together",
  "shortDescription": "A fun and friendly live session for parents to practice speaking English through real-life conversations about hobbies, home life, family, and more.",
  "description": "<p>In this session, we’ll practice real conversations that are easy, useful, and fun — helping you speak more confidently at home, in the market, or with friends and family.</p><p>Together, we’ll explore these simple but powerful topics:</p><ol><li>Talking About Hobbies and Free Time – Learn to express what you enjoy doing and ask others about their interests.</li><li>Describing Your Home – Practice how to describe your house and different rooms in English.</li><li>Talking About Your Child’s Day – Speak about school routines, subjects, and daily activities.</li><li>Making Plans with Friends or Neighbors – Learn phrases to suggest plans or invite someone politely.</li><li>Polite Requests and Offers – Use English to ask for help or offer something kindly.</li><li>Sharing Good News – Learn how to celebrate achievements and respond positively in English.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>This class will include speaking practice, roleplay, teacher feedback, and simple vocabulary support. No pressure, no tests — just real English for real life.</p><p><br></p><p>Let’s speak, smile, and support each other as we learn together!</p>",
  "time": {
    "$date": "2025-10-27T09:45:00.000Z"
  },
  "teacher": [
    {
      "$oid": "6836a841b348450b46f63fa5"
    }
  ],
  "pricing": {
    "type": "inCourse"
  },
  "seatLimit": 30,
  "cover": {
    "$oid": "68c116a6170efe97b0af61d2"
  },
  "banner": {
    "$oid": "68c116a6170efe97b0af61d2"
  },
  "topics": [
    "Talking About Hobbies and Free Time",
    "Describing Your Home",
    "Talking About Your Child’s Day",
    "Making Plans with Friends or Neighbors",
    "Polite Requests and Offers",
    "Sharing Good News"
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "title": "Who is this live class for?",
      "answer": "<p>This class is specially designed for parents who are learning basic spoken English. If you want to improve your everyday communication skills — whether at home, in the community, or with your children — this class is for you.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Do I need to speak English fluently to join?",
      "answer": "<p>Not at all! This class is for beginners and early learners. You will learn through simple sentences, real-life topics, and guided practice. Your teacher will help you step by step.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "What will I learn in this class?",
      "answer": "<p>You’ll practice speaking English about:</p><ul><li>Your hobbies and free time</li><li>Describing your home</li><li>Talking about your child’s day</li><li>Making polite requests and offers</li><li>Making plans with others</li><li>Sharing good news and happy moments</li></ul><p>These are real conversations that you can use in your daily life.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Will there be group activities?",
      "answer": "<p>Yes! You will take part in group speaking practice, roleplays, and simple interactive tasks. You don’t need to perform or be perfect — just try your best, and the teacher will guide and support you.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Do I need a microphone or camera?",
      "answer": "<p>A microphone is strongly recommended so you can practice speaking. A camera is optional, but turning it on can help make the session more interactive and personal.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Will there be materials after the class?",
      "answer": "<p>Yes. After the class, you may receive:</p><ul><li>A short vocabulary sheet</li><li>Speaking practice examples</li><li>Optional practice activities you can do at home</li></ul><p><br></p>"
    }
  ],
  "status": "expired",
  "moderator": {
